<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Debug-configuration entitlements for running on a device signed by a FREE
	  (Personal) Apple team.

	  Personal teams cannot be issued profiles containing
	  `com.apple.developer.applesignin` or
	  `com.apple.developer.devicecheck.appattest-environment` — both are paid
	  Apple Developer Program capabilities. Xcode fails with "Personal
	  development teams … do not support the Sign In with Apple and App Attest
	  capabilities" before it can build to a phone.

	  What this costs, precisely:

	  • App Attest — NOTHING in Debug. `FirebaseBootstrap` already installs
	    `AppCheckDebugProviderFactory()` under `#if DEBUG || targetEnvironment(simulator)`,
	    so App Attest is never exercised in a Debug build. The entitlement was
	    inert here.

	  • Sign In with Apple — the Apple button stops working in this build only.
	    Google and Guest sign-in are unaffected, and `AuthManager` keeps its
	    full guest path. Release builds are untouched and keep both.

	  The app group is retained: the widget, Messages and Watch extensions all
	  share `group.com.jordancoaten.noum` and break without it.

	  DELETE THIS FILE and revert the Debug `CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS` back to
	  `Noum.entitlements` once the paid programme is active, so Debug and
	  Release test the same capability set again.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.jordancoaten.noum</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
